WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Good morning John, it is Wednesday, November 3rd, "Song Wednesday", and this is a song that I wrote.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.500
It's about Phineas Gage.

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:10.900
[music]

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:15.140
Oh Phineas Gage was 25 years old in 1848

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:19.820
And he liked his job working at the railroad but he had another fate.

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:25.000
He was blastin' rock when something distracted him

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:29.720
and he forgot to put the tamping sand in.

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:34.460
And he shoved the tamping rod into that little hole onto the blasting powder

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:40.040
and suddenly his entire left frontal lobe had been turned into clam chowderrrrrrrrr...

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:45.080
Oh this is the story of Phineas Gage who was stabbed in the brain

00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:51.060
and once your frontal lobe has been destroyed you can never go home again.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:56.220
A little while later Phineas Gage was sittin' on his bed

00:00:56.460 --> 00:01:01.200
He told the doctor the tamping rod had shot straight through his head.

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:05.680
But the doctor could not believe what Phineas said

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:10.560
for if that were the case he surely would be dead.

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:16.720
But then Phineas had a coughing fit and a teacupful of brains fell out of his head

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:21.280
and that was more than the doctor could explain!

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:26.120
Oh this is the story of Phineas Gage who was stabbed in the brain

00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:32.200
and once your frontal lobe has been destroyed you can never go home again

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:37.240
Well the doctor told the family to prepare for Gage's death

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:41.600
'cuz the one you take before your head gets stabbed is usually your last breath

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:45.700
And Phineas spent the next few months in bed

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:51.560
in and out of consciousness with a swelling in his head

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:56.120
But mere months after the accident he walked right down his stairs

00:01:56.160 --> 00:02:01.800
as if having lost a quarter of his brain left him no worse for wear...

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:06.780
Oh this is the story of Phineas Gage who was stabbed in the brain

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:13.200
and once your frontal lobe has been destroyed you can never go home again

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:17.580
But, unfortunately for Phineas, our story won't end there

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:22.560
The reason we still know his name is the strangest part of this affair

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:27.380
After his brain was scrambled, his friends and family said

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:32.680
"This is no longer Phineas, there's a new man here instead"

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:37.280
And thus we know that operating on the brain need not cause death

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:43.000
And that what makes a person who he is is not the heart but the head...

00:02:43.420 --> 00:02:48.200
Oh this is the story of Phineas Gage who was stabbed in the brain

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:52.800
and once your frontal lobe has been destroyed you can never go home again...

00:02:54.180 --> 00:03:01.300
Oh Phineas Gage was 37 years old when he finally made his way back to his home and family

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:07.840
for he could tell the day of his death was finally creeping up on him

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:13.240
'cause he forgot to put the tamping sand in

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:17.700
and as is common in these cases of severe head trauma

00:03:18.140 --> 00:03:24.200
seizures took their toll and put an end to this drama.

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:30.200
Thanks to Katherine and Lemon for helping me film that video; Lemon actually didn't help at all.

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:32.980
I'm sorry we didn't think to clean the lens beforehand...

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:36.540
Sorry that I have not addressed the somewhat pressing concern of whether or not you could be my Sing-a-ma-jig player;

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:39.460
that's simply because I am not entirely sure I know how to write for Sing-a-ma-jig.

00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:41.140
Actually I think it's because I thought you were kidding.

00:03:41.140 --> 00:03:45.900
But I now that I know that you're serious I'm going to do some research and figure out whether or not I can write for Sing-a-ma-jig.

00:03:46.360 --> 00:03:47.820
John, I'll see you on Friday.

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:56.060
This is what happens when you're camera-manning and the dog is tied to you.

00:03:56.060 --> 00:03:58.020
A tumbleweed just went over my Macbook.

00:03:58.180 --> 00:04:00.020
I love Montana!

